---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, TOPICS, EXPERIENCE, EDUCATION, type Topic } from '../consts';
const topicIds = Object.keys(TOPICS) as Topic[];
const arc = [
  { year: '2020', text: 'Working with data and dashboards, I built version control for Tableau workbooks.' },
  { year: '2022', text: 'Went deeper on the foundations with data engineering coursework.' },
  { year: '2024', text: 'Rebuilt ML from first principles (linear regression), learned CI/CD from zero, and tried AI agents for risk and assurance.' },
  { year: '2026', text: 'Started learning in public: model architectures by hand, a framework per lesson on leading AI, and a privacy hackathon.' },
];
---
<Base title="About" description={`Who ${SITE.name} is, what drives the work, and how to get in touch.`}>
  <div class="narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm {SITE.short}. I like to <span class="hl">see how things work</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm someone who isn't satisfied until I can see how a thing really works. With AI, that means two things:
      understanding the models themselves, down to every matrix, and understanding how organisations can adopt
      them well. I learn both in public, and turn what I learn into material other people can use.
    </p>
    {(SITE.role || SITE.location) && <p class="muted">{[SITE.role, SITE.location].filter(Boolean).join(' · ')}</p>}

    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <ul class="topics">
      {topicIds.map((t) => (
        <li data-t={t}><span class="topic-dot" /><div><strong>{TOPICS[t].label}</strong><br /><span class="muted">{TOPICS[t].blurb}</span></div></li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>What drives the work</h2>
    <p>
      I was learning about attention, and wanted more than the equations in the paper. I wanted to see every
      matrix, know its shape at every step, and do the multiplications myself until the forward pass clicked.
      Sinusoidal positional encoding, giving every position its own signature, was the idea that hooked me.
      That became <a href="https://guptaaditya95.github.io/llmbreakdown/">Let's Break It Down</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      At the same time I'm working through a course on leading AI transformation. Rather than let notes sit in a
      notebook, I turn each lesson into a framework with a case study, in the
      <a href="https://guptaaditya95.github.io/ai-transformation-playbook/">AI Transformation Playbook</a>.
      If I can't explain it simply, I haven't understood it.
    </p>

    {EXPERIENCE.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <ul class="xp">
          {EXPERIENCE.map((x) => (
            <li><div class="top"><strong>{x.role}</strong><span class="small muted">{x.dates}</span></div><span class="muted">{x.org}</span>{x.note && <p class="small">{x.note}</p>}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    )}
    {EDUCATION.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <ul class="xp">{EDUCATION.map((e) => <li><strong>{e.what}</strong><br /><span class="muted">{e.where}{e.dates && ` · ${e.dates}`}</span></li>)}</ul>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>How my interests have grown</h2>
    <ol class="arc">
      {arc.map((a) => <li><span class="year">{a.year}</span><span>{a.text}</span></li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="small"><a href="/projects/">See every project →</a></p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is on <a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>. For corrections or ideas about a
      project, open an issue on <a href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub</a>. And if you want to learn alongside me, the
      <a href="/community/">community page</a> has the ways to join.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .topics { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .topics li { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: baseline; }
  .xp { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .xp li { padding: 0.75rem 0; border-bottom: 1.5px dashed var(--border); }
  .xp p { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; }
  .top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .arc { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.8rem 0 0; border-left: 2px dashed var(--border); }
  .arc li { display: flex; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.45rem 0 0.45rem 1rem; position: relative; }
  .arc li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: -7px; top: 0.95rem; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50% 40% 55% 45%; background: var(--hl); border: 1.5px solid var(--text); }
  .year { font-family: var(--hand); font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--accent); flex: none; width: 2.6rem; }
  .topics strong { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; }
</style>
